{
  "assessment": "The paper presents a stochastic model (A-CTRW) for colloid filtration in heterogeneous porous media, with several quantitative claims. The most central and self-contained quantitative claim is the deposition profile cutoff length L_c = (v_bar / (r_bar * k)) * (xi_0^2 / (2 * d_c)), which is explicitly given in Eq. (5) and discussed in the text. This formula can be abstracted into a closed-form oracle with controllable inputs (xi_0, d_c, k) and a readout (L_c). Other claims, such as the flight length distribution p_lambda(lambda) or the deposition profile shape, are more complex and not directly reducible to a simple closed-form expression without additional assumptions. The paper parameters for the cutoff formula are: v_bar = 0.16 mm/s (average Darcy velocity), r_bar = 0.09 mm (average grain radius, since r in [0.06,0.12] mm with P_r ~ r^{-3}, the mean is approximately 0.09 mm), xi_0 = 0.063 mm, d_c = 0.01 um = 1e-5 mm, k = 4.3e-4 s^{-1}. These yield L_c = (0.16 / (0.09 * 4.3e-4)) * (0.063^2 / (2 * 1e-5)) = (0.16 / 3.87e-5) * (0.003969 / 2e-5) = 4134.37 * 198.45 = 820,000 mm, which is far larger than the domain length (990 mm), consistent with the paper's observation that the cutoff is far away. The counterfactual changes one parameter at a time, e.g., increasing d_c to 0.1 um reduces L_c to 82,000 mm, still large but showing the inverse dependence. The oracle uses the formula with parameters as named. The diagnostic conditions vary xi_0, d_c, and k within reasonable ranges, and hidden conditions test extrapolation. The claim is abstractable under the contract.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "family": "colloid_filtration_cutoff",
      "title": "Deposition profile cutoff length in heterogeneous porous media",
      "claim": "The cutoff length of the deposition profile is given by L_c = (v_bar / (r_bar * k)) * (xi_0^2 / (2 * d_c)), where v_bar is the average flight velocity, r_bar is the average grain radius, k is the attachment rate, xi_0 is the pore size cutoff, and d_c is the critical distance for attachment.",
      "source": {
        "citation": "Filippo Miele et al., Flow-Induced Intermittent Transport Shapes Colloid Filtration in Complex Media, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/122c-f92l",
        "journal_doi": "10.1103/122c-f92l",
        "arxiv_versioned_id": "2505.02689v1",
        "locator": "Eq. (5) and Discussion section",
        "role": "derived formula"
      },
      "apparatus": {
        "name": "microfluidic_porous_medium",
        "description": "A microfluidic chip with a heterogeneous porous structure of cylindrical grains, used to measure colloid deposition profiles."
      },
      "background": "In heterogeneous porous media, colloid transport is intermittent, with particles alternating between flights (far from surfaces) and dives (near surfaces). The deposition profile exhibits a power-law near the inlet and an exponential cutoff at large distances. The cutoff length L_c is predicted by a stochastic model and depends on medium structure and attachment kinetics.",
      "initial_observations": [
        "Deposition profiles show a power-law decay near the inlet and an exponential cutoff at larger distances.",
        "The cutoff length L_c is observed to be much larger than the flight length cutoff.",
        "Increasing the critical distance d_c decreases L_c, while increasing the pore size cutoff xi_0 extends the power-law regime."
      ],
      "controls": [
        {
          "name": "xi_0",
          "description": "Cutoff pore size in the pore size distribution",
          "unit": "mm",
          "minimum": 0.01,
          "maximum": 0.2
        },
        {
          "name": "d_c",
          "description": "Critical distance from grain surface for attachment",
          "unit": "mm",
          "minimum": 1e-6,
          "maximum": 1e-3
        },
        {
          "name": "k",
          "description": "Attachment rate",
          "unit": "1/s",
          "minimum": 1e-5,
          "maximum": 1e-2
        }
      ],
      "readouts": [
        {
          "name": "L_c",
          "description": "Cutoff length of the deposition profile",
          "unit": "mm",
          "resolution": 0.1
        }
      ],
      "oracle": {
        "kind": "closed_form",
        "outputs": {
          "L_c": {
            "op": "multiply",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "divide",
                "args": [
                  {"param": "v_bar"},
                  {
                    "op": "multiply",
                    "args": [
                      {"param": "r_bar"},
                      {"var": "k"}
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "divide",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "power",
                    "args": [
                      {"var": "xi_0"},
                      2
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "multiply",
                    "args": [
                      2,
                      {"var": "d_c"}
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "paper_parameters": {
          "v_bar": 0.16,
          "r_bar": 0.09
        },
        "counterfactual_parameters": {
          "v_bar": 0.16,
          "r_bar": 0.09
        }
      },
      "diagnostic_conditions": [
        {
          "xi_0": 0.063,
          "d_c": 1e-5,
          "k": 4.3e-4
        },
        {
          "xi_0": 0.063,
          "d_c": 1e-4,
          "k": 4.3e-4
        },
        {
          "xi_0": 0.1,
          "d_c": 1e-5,
          "k": 4.3e-4
        },
        {
          "xi_0": 0.063,
          "d_c": 1e-5,
          "k": 1e-3
        }
      ],
      "hidden_conditions": [
        {
          "xi_0": 0.05,
          "d_c": 5e-5,
          "k": 2e-4
        },
        {
          "xi_0": 0.08,
          "d_c": 2e-5,
          "k": 8e-4
        }
      ],
      "budget": 10,
      "max_replicates": 3,
      "confidence_threshold": 0.95,
      "relative_tolerance": 0.1,
      "notes": [
        "The formula is derived from the A-CTRW model and validated against experiments.",
        "The paper parameters reproduce the experimental cutoff, which is much larger than the domain length.",
        "Counterfactual changes alter one parameter at a time to explore sensitivity."
      ],
      "counterfactual_change": "Increase d_c from 1e-5 mm to 1e-4 mm, keeping other parameters fixed."
    }
  ]
}
